Z||000000||Mattyman||11-03-2001||07:42 PM||||Well it could have been dangerous but it turned out funny.  Back when I use to drive my parnets vehicles, I got the urge to joke around and make a joke out of my dads Astro Van,  called the 'STRO, so me and my friend put racing stripes on it and a few other things.  Remember this is just a joke so i could mess around with the ricers.  And man is it funny.  If you want to laugh go to  <A HREF="http://www.3strosalute.8m.com" TARGET=_blank>www.3strosalute.8m.com</A>    <BR>and take a look at it.<BR>Well today my dad went out with a friend to pick up some chairs.  He had the trailer on and while he was going he got a flat, it would of been nice if he had a spare tire, but it fell out from underneith the van when I was driving one day.  The chain thing holding it rusted away and the rim was all rusty. Well the rim was at our house for some reason, so my dad called our neighbor up to bring the spare so he could take the van to the local garage/gas station to get it fixed.  He made it there on the old crappy spare tire, thats a miracle in its self.  They couldn't patch the tire with the hole, but they had one that was the right size which had a hole in it so they patched that hole and put the tire on the van.  Well my dad and his friend drove around for awhile transporting the chairs.  Then my dad noticed that something felt weird like a tire was flat so his friend got out and checked and all the tires looked fine.  So they contined to drive. About 100 yards down the road, the front drivers side tire that they fixed flew off into some guys yard and the stro slid off the road on the rotor for about 30 yards. There is a nice scratch in the road from the rotor scraping.  Well i got there in my fiero(dont ask how, its a story in its self) and I was like what the heck happened.  I checked out the tire and it was all bored out where the lug nuts go.  And the lugnuts were laying back on the road somewhere. My dad called AAA and they were coming with a tow truck and my neighbor was coming to tow the trailer back to our house.  Me and my dads good friend drove back to the service station which was only about a mile away and told the guy what happened and the idiot laughed.  What he did was he put the tire on wrong, it wasnt up against some inner rim thing on the rotor or something so he thought he tightened it up but it was no where near it.  They ended up taking responsibilty for it, which is real suprising, and they fixed everything.  But the 'STRO has an old black rim on it.  They are looking for one like the origionals and going to put it on.  If they cant find one, I'm going to get them to buy me new rims for my Fiero.  Hahaha, ya right. Well next time that you go to get stuff done with your tires or anything on your car, check to see if its done right, people make mistakes, some dont admit it but its nice that others do and try to fix it.||||reg||10
